  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with a history of transient cerebral ischemic attacks (G45.9) and unspecified cardiac arrhythmia (I49.9), reporting intermittent episodes of dizziness and palpitations that are poorly correlated with standard ECG findings. A cardiac event monitoring study (CPT 93271) is clinically indicated to evaluate for paroxysmal atrial fibrillation or other intermittent dysrhythmias that may be contributing to these transient neurological symptoms. This specific monitoring is necessary to identify the underlying cause of the patient's symptoms, which cannot be adequately assessed by standard ECG alone."
